        "original_id": "1ecdd3a5-5a9f-576d-a300-92d91f14a765",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paola Suárez, Virginia Ruano Pascual, Michael Venus, Chan Hao-ching, Monica Niculescu, Max Mirnyi, Ashleigh Barty, John Peers\n- Sports: professional tennis, doubles, mixed doubles, women's doubles\n- Events: Wimbledon 2017, US Open 2014, US Open 2017\n- Rankings: WTA/ATP doubles No. 1, singles ranking\n\nFacts:\n- Paola Suárez was born on 23 June 1976 and is a retired professional tennis player from Argentina.\n- Michael Venus reached a career-high singles ranking of 274 in July 2011.\n- At the 2014 US Open mixed doubles event, Max Mirnyi and Chan Hao-ching lost in the second round to Ashleigh Barty and John Peers.\n- In 2017, Chan Hao-ching reached the Wimbledon women's doubles final with Monica Niculescu.\n- In 2017, Chan Hao-ching reached the US Open mixed doubles final with Michael Venus.\n- During the early and mid-2000s, Paola Suárez was one of the most prominent women's doubles players.\n- Paola Suárez won eight Grand Slam titles in doubles, all with Virginia Ruano Pascual.\n- Paola Suárez held the No. 1 doubles ranking for 87 non-consecutive weeks.\n- Michael Venus is better known as a leading doubles player with a huge serve.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7f4e76b2-da1d-54b0-9060-5ff12af3d47f",
        "text": "Page: Paola Suárez. Sentence: Paola Suárez (born 23 June 1976) is a retired professional tennis player from Argentina.\nPage: Paola Suárez. Sentence: She was one of the most prominent women's doubles players throughout the early and mid-2000s, winning eight Grand Slam titles, all of them with Virginia Ruano Pascual, and holding the No. 1 doubles ranking for 87 non-consecutive weeks.\nPage: Michael Venus (tennis). Sentence: He reached a career high singles ranking of 274 in July 2011, but is much better known as a leading doubles player with a huge serve.\nPage: Chan Hao-ching. Sentence: She reached two more in 2017: the women's doubles at Wimbledon with Monica Niculescu, and the US Open mixed doubles with Michael Venus.\nPage: 2014 US Open – Mixed Doubles. Sentence: Mirnyi teamed up with Chan Hao-ching, but lost in the second round to Ashleigh Barty and John Peers.",
